Z||000002||btoth||07-05-2001||07:18 PM||||Focus' really need some larger rear wheels to balance out that huge rear-end.<P>When will the huge rear-end trend die?  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I prefer being able to <I>see</I> what's behind me while I'm backing up.  (Just my opinion.)||||reg||1
Z||000003||rogergarrison||07-05-2001||09:07 PM||||I hate those too. I like car lines to have some length at the trunk to balance it. They have to make the short ones tall to give you any kind of usuable trunk. And that also makes the rear wheels look tiny on the car, just like it did on Mustang. They need at least 18'' rims in rear to make it look right. Otherwise I think they look like 'HotWheels' toys. On Fieros, I personally think the rear is too short too (Id like lots more trunk space) and the wheel openings way too big unless you stick some big wheels on it.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Slammed Fiero||07-05-2001||09:38 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/prot5.gif"> <P>My screamin yellow banna looks better. I like this little car. Needs a turbo of course, but this little sucker has potential!<P><BR>I have looked at getting and SVT focus (my uncle has an SVT dealership) but since you said it's no easily upgradeable I have steered clear of the idea.<P>PErhaps I will find a nice mid 90's 240, you can buy a used skyline for 30 grand Hmmmm<P>JM ||||reg||1
Z||000005||Shaft||07-06-2001||12:01 AM||||Slammed: I like the look of the new Mazda's too...but only 120 hp?! Yeah a turbo would definately be nice on that.<P>Also, you mentioned a mid 90's 240. Hopefully you mean the S13 Hatchback Body. In my opinion those are the best looking 240' out there. My friend has a 93 that is still stock and it can still beat most stock cars (with the exception of VTEC preludes and some Integras). His goal is to get enough money to do the SR20DET engine conversion. For those of you that don't know, that's the engine that was in that car in Japan (there it's called the Silvia) the newer versions have 250hp and can be put in a 240 relatively easily. Also since the Silvia used the same body as the 240 there is plenty of room up front for a very large intercooler. People who ave done this conversion can run high 12's or low 13's with no other mods to the engine.||||reg||1
