Z||000015||Tevlin Arkady||07-24-2001||10:50 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Fformula88:<BR><B>$24,000 for a Focus?!?!?  WTF!!  That is absolutely rediculous.  I don't care if it had a Contour SVT V6!  I still wouldn't give Ford that kind of money for one.<P>For that kind of money, you can be cruising in a Miata with the top down, blowing away from the Focus from the stoplight and in the twisties, and have lots of change left over for gas and dinner!</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>A new miata up here in Canada is approaching 40 grand. I also believe that a Miata and a Focus  with the better motor are even in performance. Where as the Focus SVT due to come out in sept. will be quite a bit quicker than a miata and around 30 grand tax in. here in Canada. <P>TA<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||Fierokid87||07-24-2001||10:56 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by fierobaby:<BR><B> I must agree the sucker has some potential! but you need to make it really look like abannanna get a chiquita bannanna decal and stick it on the side!!! <P>Corinne<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P><BR>Yes I agree with Corinne.  "chiquita bannanna" decal would look great on it.<P>Scott<BR><P>------------------<BR><FONT COLOR="BLOODY"> Fierokid's  Web site<BR>http://www.angelfire.com/sports/sfiero<P>AIM: Fierokid87<BR>ICQ: Fierokid</FONT><P>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sfiero.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||Fformula88||07-24-2001||04:49 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Tevlin Arkady:<BR><B> A new miata up here in Canada is approaching 40 grand. I also believe that a Miata and a Focus  with the better motor are even in performance. Where as the Focus SVT due to come out in sept. will be quite a bit quicker than a miata and around 30 grand tax in. here in Canada. <P>TA<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>This car isn't in Canada and neither am I.  So obviously Canadian pricing has no effect on my buying habits.  Also, this isn't a Focus SVT, it has a stock motor.<P>As for handling, this particular Focus probably handles well with its wheel/tire upgrade (and possible other suspension ugrades).  Its hard to tell what it would do vs a Miata, but I would seriously doubt it could be substantially better.  That combined with the weak Zetec, hands down Miata wins.<P>The Focus SVT is a different subject.  Its going to have a 170 HP, 145 lb-ft Torque Zetec engine.  Estimates predict its 0-60 times to be in the 7 second range.  Hmmm, the Miata hits 60 in 7.5 sec.  Quite a bit quicker?  doubtful.  The SVT will have a few more ponies, but its got more bulk to haul around too.<P>To the SVT's advantage in the price war will be an $18,500 estimated price.  So for pure bang for the buck it looks to be a better choice.<P>I still say Miata is more appealing.  Although performance looks close between the two, the Miata is a better looking (IMO), and a Convertible vs an econobox-looking hatchback.||||reg||1
Z||000018||1FST2M6||07-24-2001||04:56 PM||||owning a miata myself and driving any others M1, and M2s, and driving many stock and modded foci, the miata is way for FUN to drive.. the SHM Focus will out handle a stock miata anyday (even teh a but the fun factor just isnt' there.. the option of over steer on the miata is there.. where the focus you have to force over steer and you can't sustain it. as for go.. they are about the same. (SLOW) a stock GT will pull a miata or a focus all day.  but the top down drift through the corner at 60+ and 25+mpg is just fun. ||||reg||1
Z||000019||California Kid||07-24-2001||05:35 PM||||Sure justifies the money I put into my GT.||||reg||6
